只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Enable passkeys in WebView-shell browsers (Via, Quark, ...) via the official androidx.webkit switch — LSPosed module; targets older WebView (~124-13x) where WebAuthn is not default-enabled; fully reversible","id":"gh:1359087786","install_available":false,"language":"Java","name":"webauthn-for-webview-shells","slug":"cmyfqwq/webauthn-for-webview-shells","topics":["android","dsh-plugin","lsposed","mit","passkeys","webauthn","webview","xposed"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Enable passkeys in WebView-shell browsers (Via, Quark, ...) via the official androidx.webkit switch "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"— LSPosed module; targets older WebView (~124-13x) where WebAuthn is not default-enabled; fully reve"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"sed module; targets older WebView (~124-13x) where WebAuthn is not default-enabled; fully reversible"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# 🔑 WebAuthn for WebView Shells"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Enable passkeys in lightweight WebView-based browsers — via the *official* androidx.webkit switch,"},{"id":"p3s2","text":" flipped from the inside.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English · 简体中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## 🧠 What this actually is"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Passkeys are already inside Android's **system WebView**. The official guideline says every host app"},{"id":"p6s2","text":" that embeds a WebView must opt in itself:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Lightweight \"shell\" browsers (Via, Quark, X, and dozens more) render every page through the system W"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ebView — but **none of them make this call**, so `navigator.credentials()` never reaches the credent"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ial stack. The capability is already there; the switch is simply never flipped."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"**This module flips it, without touching native app code.** It is a small LSPosed module that hooks "},{"id":"p9s2","text":"`WebView` construction inside target browsers and applies the official integration on their behalf, "},{"id":"p9s3","text":"backed by its own copy of `androidx.webkit`."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"> No patching of the system password manager · no network I/O · no UI injection.\n> **Revert = flip t"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"he module off in LSPosed. That's it.**"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## ✅ What you get"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- Your website now realizes the phone has a platform authenticator.\n- Creating and verifying passkey"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"s goes through the **native password manager** (ColorOS 密码本, One UI Passcodes, Google Password Manag"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"er…)\n- The module keeps gluing itself back on whenever the host re-touches its settings."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## 🧱 Tech stack"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| Layer | What | Why |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| Hook runtime | **Xposed API 93 / LSPosed** | injects into the browser's own process; module off = "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"stock behavior |\n| Bridge | **androidx.webkit 1.17** (`WebSettingsCompat.setWebAuthenticationSupport"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"`) | the official WebView ↔ Credential-Manager integration; shipped inside the module dex |\n| Target"},{"id":"p16s4","text":" floor | **Android 7.0+ (API 24), System WebView 124+** | device must already carry WebAuthn-capable"},{"id":"p16s5","text":" WebView; module enables, never backports |\n| Build | **javac → d8 → aapt2 → apksigner** (plain Powe"},{"id":"p16s6","text":"rShell, no Gradle) | ~350 lines total; everything reproducible from one script |\n| Depends on nothin"},{"id":"p16s7","text":"g else | no network, no UI, no system writes | reversibility is the design constraint |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"> Why ship our own androidx.webkit? Because the shells never bundle it — the hook must supply the br"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"idge library it is applying."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## 📦 Shell support"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| Browser | Status |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| **Via GP** (`mark.via.gp` 7.3.3) | ✅ tested — passkey **create + verify** work with the native pas"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"sword manager |\n| **Via CN** (`mark.via`) | wired & installed by default; needs nothing but your own"},{"id":"p20s3","text":" test |\n| *Everything else* | ⚠️ supports this mechanism (WebView ≥ 124), but **not wired by default"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"** — add the package name to `TARGETS` in `MainHook.java`, rebuild, and try it out |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## 🕓 Compatibility: is it even needed on your device?"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"**Maybe not — check before reporting \"no effect\".** The module exists because WebView used to keep W"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"ebAuthn off by default unless the host opted in. Newer WebView / OS builds have started flipping tha"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"t default themselves:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| Your device situation | What you'll see |"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| **Android ≤ 16, WebView ~124–13x** (historical default: opt-in required) | ✅ module's sweet spot —"},{"id":"p24s2","text":" without it, shell browsers report \"no platform authenticator\" |\n| **Android 16/17 with a recent Web"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"View** (observed: HyperOS 4.0.0.24, Android 17, WebView past 124) | ⚠️ WebView may already enable `n"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"avigator.credentials` for shells by default — the module becomes a **no-op redundancy** on those dev"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"ices; passkey success there comes from the credential provider side, not this hook |\n| Shell that ca"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"lls the androidx switch itself | ✅ any version — module is redundant by design (that's the goal) |"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Quick self-check: disable the module in LSPosed, force-stop the browser, retry passkeys. If they sti"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"ll work, your device no longer needs this module — nothing is broken."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Also note the provider side: on Xiaomi HyperOS 4 the default credential provider may still reject We"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"bView-originated requests (`NotReadableError`); see FAQ / 中文 FAQ."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## 🚀 Install"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"1. Requires: **rooted device + LSPosed**, Android 7.0+, system WebView **124+**\n2. Download the APK "},{"id":"p28s2","text":"from Releases, install it\n3. Enable the module in **LSPosed Manager** (scope is pre-filled from the "},{"id":"p28s3","text":"manifest) and restart your browser\n4. Open any passkey-capable site and watch the system sheet appea"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"anifest) and restart your browser\n4. Open any passkey-capable site and watch the system sheet appear"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"**This module is fully reversible** — turn it off or `pm uninstall io.github.cmyfqwq.webauthnshell`;"},{"id":"p29s2","text":" everything returns to stock with no residue."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## 🔨 Build it yourself"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"No Gradle needed — a plain PowerShell script drives `javac → d8 → aapt2 → apksigner` from any Androi"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"dle needed — a plain PowerShell script drives `javac → d8 → aapt2 → apksigner` from any Android SDK:"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"Want another browser? Add its package to `TARGETS` in\n`MainHook.java` and rebuild."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## 🧭 FAQ"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"**Is this an exploit?**\nNo. It sets a public (androidx) setting inside the target app's own process "},{"id":"p35s2","text":"— exactly what the shell could call itself. Nothing is added to a WebView it cannot already do, and "},{"id":"p35s3","text":"system WebView gatekeepers stay untouched."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"**Why not ask the browsers upstream?**\nPlease do — a 3-line change in each browser would obsolete th"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"is module, which is the ideal outcome. This module exists to close the gap until then."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## ☕ Credits"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"- Built on the official `androidx.webkit` WebView–Credential-Manager bridge\n- Problem coverage gathe"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"red from the caniuse passkey matrix (QQ 14.9 / Baidu 13.52 unsupported) and in-app-shell breakage re"},{"id":"p38s3","text":"ported upstream, e.g. openai/codex #31204"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"**:fox:')\nbuilt by cmyfqwq · MIT · no tracking, no network, one switch**"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
